            <div xml:id="d472">

                <pb facs="0640" n="546" sameAs="frus:frus1924v02/pg546"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">891.51/340: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Persia</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Kornfeld</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Teheran</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1924-05-15T16:00:00+03:25"><hi rendition="#italic">May 15, 1924—4
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received May 15—10:54
                    a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>40. British Government has telegraphed its Chargé here that it cannot consent to
                    hypothecation of Anglo-Persian royalties and southern customs for loan in United
                    States before a settlement has been reached concerning Persian debts to Great
                    Britain.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kornfeld</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
